# kanshi — output geometry. Every profile below is the CLIENT's (the ASUS
# Zenbook Duo UX8406MA, the fleet's only seat since 2026-09-11). The file is a
# fleet-wide raw symlink (home/home.nix configDirs), so it is deployed
# everywhere, but no other host matches a profile in it and none is wanted:
# the coordinator is headless (DECISIONS.md 2026-09-11) and the worker and nas
# have no seat.
#
# THE CLIENT HAS EXACTLY TWO DISPLAYS, its own two 14-inch 2880x1800 OLED
# panels: eDP-1 (top) and eDP-2 (bottom, under the detachable keyboard). Both
# are lit whenever the keyboard is off. The Thunderbolt dock carries hubs, a
# NIC and peripherals and NO display — DP-1, DP-2 and HDMI-A-1 all read
# `disconnected` on the metal (2026-09-13). The two `DuoDock*` profiles that
# used to sit above these, matching an "ASUS PA27JCV" by description string,
# could never have applied and are gone; Tom's note on this file (2026-09-12:
# "it's NOT the asus pa27 it's a 14 inch display") is what caught it, and
# DECISIONS.md 2026-09-13 records the correction. If a display is ever plugged
# into the dock, no profile here matches and niri's own defaults govern — add
# a measured profile then, not a guess now.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. kanshi applies the FIRST profile whose output set matches the
# connected set exactly (kanshi(5)); the two sets below are disjoint, so order
# is only a habit here: both panels first, then one.
#
# The keyboard axis: modules/zenbook-duo-daemon.nix forces eDP-2's DRM status
# to `off` when the physical keyboard is snapped over the bottom panel, and
# back `on` when it is lifted. kanshi sees a real hotplug either way, so
# "…Docked" here means KEYBOARD-docked — one eDP — not dock-station-docked.
#
# Outputs are matched by CONNECTOR name (stable: the Duo's own eDP-1/eDP-2).

profile Duo {
    output eDP-1 scale 2 position 0,0   adaptive_sync on
    output eDP-2 scale 2 position 0,900 adaptive_sync on
    exec busctl --user set-property rs.wl-gammarelay /outputs/eDP_1 rs.wl.gammarelay Temperature q 3850
    exec busctl --user set-property rs.wl-gammarelay /outputs/eDP_2 rs.wl.gammarelay Temperature q 3350
}

profile DuoDocked {
    output eDP-1 scale 2 position 0,0 adaptive_sync on
    exec busctl --user set-property rs.wl-gammarelay /outputs/eDP_1 rs.wl.gammarelay Temperature q 3850
}
